<title>USA: OppenheimerFunds fund manager Rosenberg resigns.</title>
<headline>OppenheimerFunds fund manager Rosenberg resigns.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>OppenheimerFunds Inc said Wednesday that David Rosenberg, one of the portfolio managers of the Oppenheimer Multi-Sector Income Trust and the Oppenheimer World Bond Fund, had resigned.</p>
<p>The company said his responsibilities on the funds are being assumed by Jerry Webman, senior vice-president and director of Tax Exempt Fixed Income Investments.</p>
<p>OppenheimerFunds Inc is the investment advisor to the Oppenheimer Funds. It is not related to Oppenheimer &amp; Co, the broker/dealer, or its affiliate Oppenheimer Capital LP.</p>
</text>
